('cso-khushi-baby-97ae67fe', 'Khushi Baby', 'Khushi Baby is a health-tech nonprofit leveraging digital and wearable technology to strengthen last-mile maternal and child health systems, especially in rural India.', 'Khushibaby about us OVERVIEW OUR VALUES OUR STORY OUR Team RECOGNITION & AWARDS REPORTS & FINANCIALS our work What we do Digital Platforms HEALTH PROGRAMS Climate and Health Partners OUR MODEL OPERATING MODEL CHIP PLATFORM HEALTH ACTION CENTERS our impact OVERVIEW THEORY OF CHANGE Publications Get involved Careers Fellowship Events Donate Delivering Khushi to the Last Mile By strengthening community health systems Overview Annual Report ABOUT US Khushi Baby is a 10-year old digital health non-profit with expertise in building solutions for health departments . Our solutions have been used by 75K community health workers to reach 48M people, supported by $20M in Ministry of Health funding. Our 90 member team has spent 250K hours co-developing solutions with health workers at the last mile. Learn More PROBLEM Community health workers lose time reporting data disconnected from last mile service delivery. ASHA workers like Bharti spend 50 hours every month, recording the services they provided on 10 registers and 5 mobile applications. Across India they spend 50M hours every month to feed data into 50 portals. Data quality is affected limiting insights that can be used to uplift the co', 'North India', null, null, null, 'India', 'contact@khushibaby.org', '345441-2488', 'https://www.khushibaby.org', '{"linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/posts/neerajjain2_climatexhealth-activity-7043551745481863168-WeX_/?utm_source=share&utm_medium=member_desktop", "twitter": "https://twitter.com/teamkhushibaby"}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Digital Health', 'Maternal & Child Health', 'Data Systems', 'North India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Digital Health', 'Maternal & Child Health', 'Data Systems', 'North India', 'Grassroot