('cso-urban-management-centre-6321e1f4', 'Urban Management Centre', 'Urban Management Centre (UMC) is a women-led non-profit advancing climate change resilience, Gov-Tech solutions, WASH services, and women''s economic empowerment. We collaborate with governments to strengthen urban governance, drive policy reforms, and build sustainable, inclusive cities. Explore our impact in capacity building, urban planning, and community-driven development.', 'UMC | Climate Change, Capacity Building, Improved Health to Women''s Empowerment top of page Home About UMC Our Initiatives Capacity Building @ LBSNAA Climate Action & Urban Resilience GovTech for Inclusive Cities Quneiform - Real Data. Real Impact. Resources Blogs Work with Us Contact Us More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Building Capacities and Shaping Inclusive Cities Established in 1997 as the Indian project office for the International City/County Management Association (ICMA), UMC has spent the past 25 years transforming the field of urban management in India and beyond. As a women-led non-profit organisation, UMC is dedicated to shaping more inclusive and resilient cities through its expertise and commitment to making cities work for everyone. Dive into Our Legacy Climate Change Gov-Tech Capacity Building Learn More Women''s Economic Empowerment Heritage Management Key Focus Areas Bridging Policy with Ground Level Insights We believe that if policy reforms are implemented; systems are strengthened; city managers are capacitated and empowered then cities would become cleaner, livable, productive and equitable. We operate across all four levels of governance-Commun', 'IN', 'Indianapolis, IN, US', 'IN', null, 'India', 'info@umcasia.org', '2545352419', 'https://home.umcasia.org', '{"youtube": "https://www.youtube.com/@UrbanManagementCentre/videos", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/urbanmanagementcentre", "x": "https://x.com/umcasia", "instagram": "https://www.instagram.com/urban_management_centre", "facebook": "https://www.facebook.com/umcasia"}'::jsonb, '["A documentation of Odisha''s Garima Programme, India''s first state-wide initiative ensuring safety, dignity, and welfare for sanitation workers.", "A-202, GCP Business Center, Opp Navrangpura Fire Station, 120 Feet Ring Rd, Sarvottam Nagar Society, Navrangpura, Ahmedabad, Gujarat 380009"]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Urban Governance', 'WASH', 'Gender Inclusion', 'Capacity Building', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Urban Governance', 'WASH', 'Gender Inclusion', 'Capacity Building', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'Urban Management Centre']::text[], 39.831706, -86.240447, 'CRA Partner Map workbook', 'https://home.umcasia.org', '{"areas_of_work": ["Urban Governance", "WASH", "Gender Inclusion", "Capacity Building"], "beneficiary_groups": ["Women", "Communities"], "geography_served": ["Pan-India", "India"], "registration_status": "Society", "registration_number": null, "programs": "UMC | Climate Change, Capacity Building, Improved Health to Women''s Empowerment top of page Home About UMC Our Initiatives Capacity Building @ LBSNAA Climate Action & Urban Resilience GovTech for Inclusive Cities Quneiform - Real Data.", "volunteer_or_partner_needs": null}'::jsonb, 'CRA partner import', 'tanmay@greenruraleconomy.in', 'Source workbook category: Grassroot/Implementation CSOs
