('cso-the-nature-conservancy-india-4aeadb21', 'The Nature Conservancy India', 'TNC India applies science-led, nature-based solutions to address climate change, water security, and biodiversity loss.', 'The Nature Conservancy India Skip to content Donate About Us About Us Who We Are How We Work Where We Work in India Our People Our Accountability Our Mission, Vision and Values What We Do What We Do Our Priorities Provide Food and Water Sustainably Protect and Restore Wild Habitats Build Healthy Cities Support Renewable Energy Our Insights Publications Stories in India Support Us Support Us Contact Us Show search Sign Up Donate Search The Nature Conservancy Sibling Symmetry Two young adult tiger cubs rest in the early morning light at Tadoba Andhari Tiger Reserve, India. © Anay Tarnekar/TNC Photo Contest 2019 About Us We are the largest conservation organisation in the world, working to protect the lands and waters on which all life depends. Learn More Our Vision We envision a vibrant and healthy India that is guided by sound science to manage its natural resources. Our global mission is to conserve the lands and waters on which all life depends. Our global vision is a world where the diversity of life thrives, and people act to conserve nature for its own sake and its ability to fulfill our needs and enrich our lives. Crown Of Himalaya Himalaya 17-07-2019 © Harris Cahyadi/TNC Phot', 'West Bengal', 'Aerial view of people bathing in West Bengal, India.', null, 'West Bengal', 'India', 'incontact@tnc.org', '1778408216', 'https://www.tncindia.in', '{"facebook": "https://www.facebook.com/thenatureconservancy", "instagram": "https://www.instagram.com/nature_org", "twitter": "https://twitter.com/nature_org", "x": "https://x.com/intent/tweet?text=Mammals,%20wildlife%20trade%20and%20the%20next%20global%20pandemic%20https://www.tncindia.in/what-we-do/our-insights/stories-in-india/wildlife-trade-and-the-next-pandemic", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/cws/share?mini=true&ur