('cso-adavi-trust-81bde3bd', 'Adavi Trust', 'Adavi Trust works for sustainable forest-based livelihoods and conservation through collaboration with indigenous communities.', 'About | Adavi Trust top of page About Themes All projects Meet the Team News & Publications Adavi Dialogues Get in touch More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. About Us We believe that everyone can be empowered to champion the wild. Adavi literally translates to `forest'' or `wilderness'' in three South Indian languages. At Adavi we are determined to aid the conservation of India''s fast disappearing natural landscapes. We create practical grass-root based interventions grounded in deep ecological philosophy to promote wildlife conservation, education, and sustainability. Adavi believes that conservation should be led by local communities and guided by science if and when required. A balanced, fair and just approach to conserving our wildlife is the need of the hour and something we strive towards. At Adavi we practice a hands-on approach on a daily basis in an off-grid field station surrounded by forests, fields, and savannah grasslands. Our Field Station The Adavi field station is a vibrant oasis situated in the Rayalaseema region of Andhra Pradesh. We are humbled to be part of an ecosystem built over millennia in the world''s oldest volcanic plateau - the Deccan plateau.', 'South India', null, null, null, 'India', '605a7baede844d278b89dc95ae0a9123@sentry-next.wixpress.com', '2545352419', 'https://www.adavitrust.org', '{"instagram": "https://www.instagram.com/the.arugu", "facebook": "https://www.facebook.com/adavitrust"}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Forest Conservation', 'Livelihoods', 'Indigenous Rights', 'South India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Forest Conservation', 'Livelihoods', 'Indigenous Rights', 'South India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'Adavi Trust']::text[], 22.3511148, 78.6677428, 'CRA Partner Map workbook', 'https: