Reviewed pages: https://www.coexistenceconsortium.com; https://www.coexistenceconsortium.com/aboutus; https://www.coexistenceconsortium.com/how; https://www.coexistenceconsortium.com/outreach; https://www.coexistenceconsortium.com/contact', 'approved', now(), 'admin', false, 'Co-existence Consortium A multi-institutional collective promoting research, communication, and policy for coexistence between people and wildlife. Coexistence | Coexistence Consortium top of page About Us Members Coexistence Resources by Our Members Fellowship Coexistence Fellows 2022 Cohort Coexistence Fellows 2023 Cohort Fellowship Bulletin Champions Coexistence Champions 2025 Cohort Outreach Webinars Blog Newsletters BLR Exhibition Connect More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Coexistence is an attempt to rethink the dominant conservation paradigm - not just protecting wild animals locked away in far-off pockets of forests, but also coexisting and living well with animals and nature around us. We are a consortium of ecologists, anthropologists, geographers and conservationists with extensive knowledge and experience in human-wildlife coexistence who have come together to promote the concept of coexistence. The focal activity of this consortium is to gain deeper insights into coexistence between humans and nature by supporting a range of context-specific coexistence projects around the world. The initial funding to set up the Coexistence Consortium came from the Lantana Elephants Exhibitions happening around the world, titled "Coexistence" and celebrating the human-nature connection. Latest Updates Coexistence in Pan-India, India India Human-Wildlife Coexistence Research Advocacy Pan-India India Networks/Alliances CRA Partner Map workbook Human-Wildlife Coexistence Research Advocacy Pan-India India Networks/Alliances Co-existence Consortium Human-Wildlife Coexistence Research Advocacy Pan-India India Society Coexistence | Coexistence Consortium top of page About Us Members Coexist