('cso-the-shola-trust-f95c1055', 'The Shola Trust', 'A non-profit organization conserving biodiversity and restoring ecosystems in the Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve through research and community action.', 'About Us | TSTwebsite _2026 top of page The Shola Trust Working for coexistence Landing Page More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. Log In Our Story Fifteen Years of Coexistence The Shola Trust was founded on the idea that conservation must be mainstream, rooted in the conversations of tea shops and local streets rather than just academic halls. Over the past decade and a half, we have transformed from a nature education collective into a multi-disciplinary conservation force. Now a team of over 300, we work at the cutting edge of human-elephant coexistence across the Nilgiri Biosphere Reserve and beyond. Our evolution reflects the urgency of our mission: moving from awareness to action. By combining local wisdom with modern science-through drone mapping, habitat restoration, and humane barriers-we are writing a new chapter for the Nilgiris where the forest and its people thrive together. Reach out to us The Shola Trust , Aloor Road, Thorappaly, Mudumalai Tiger Reserve, Nilgiris Info@thesholatrust.org bottom of page', 'South India', null, null, null, 'India', 'info@thesholatrust.org', '2545352419', 'https://www.thesholatrust.org/', '{}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Biodiversity Conservation', 'Restoration', 'Community Engagement', 'South India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Biodiversity Conservation', 'Restoration', 'Community Engagement', 'South India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'The Shola Trust']::text[], 22.3511148, 78.6677428, 'CRA Partner Map workbook', 'https://www.thesholatrust.org/', '{"areas_of_work": ["Biodiversity Conservation", "Restoration", "Community Engagement"], "beneficiary_groups": ["Communities"], "geography_served": ["South India"], "registration_status": "Trust", "registration_numbe