('cso-pragati-abhiyan-935324d4', 'Pragati Abhiyan', 'Pragati Abhiyan breaks the poverty trap through MGNREGA facilitation, sustainable livelihoods, and social legislation for marginalized rural families in India.', 'Pragati Abhiyan pamanage456@gmail.com +91 76667 21411 मराठी English मराठी मराठी English मराठी Home About Us Our Inspiration Our Vision - Mission Our Board Our Team Annual Reports Legal & Financial Compliance Our Work Strengthening MGNREGA Sustainable Livelihoods Revival of Millets Grain Processing Units Bamboo-based Livelihood Livestock Community Forest Rights Climate Adaptation Working with Institutions Collaborations Capacity Building Networking & Advocacy Associates Resources Our Publications Programme Reports Research Reports MGNREGA Reports Governance Reports Newspaper Articles Radio Programmes Videos Contact Us Join as Volunteer/Intern Request A Training Contact Join Now Donate Now Join Now Donate Now The Issue More poor live in rural India than in urban areas Most rural poor are typically either landless or small landholders with no irrigation facilities. Lack of access to productive resources together with structural marginalisation puts them into the poverty trap. Here comes the role of social legislations to promote and protect the rights of people and upgrade their well-being and quality of life. India has landmark legislations, such as Mahatma Gandhi National Rural Empl', 'Nashik, Maharashtra', 'Bramhand Bunglow, Deepali Nagar - Vinay Nagar Rd, Deepali Nagar, Nashik, Maharashtra 422009', 'Nashik', 'Maharashtra', 'India', 'pamanage456@gmail.com', '+917666721411', 'https://pragatiabhiyan.org/', '{"youtube": "https://www.youtube.com/@pragatiabhiyan-nashik5439"}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Governance', 'Livelihoods', 'Poverty Alleviation', 'West India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Governance', 'Livelihoods', 'Poverty Alleviation', 'West India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'Pragati Abhiyan']::