('cso-inrem-37fafb21', 'INREM', 'Breaking down government schemes like Jal Jeevan Mission and water quality standards into easy-to-understand guides for communities and organisations.', 'INREM Foundation - INREM Foundation Home Programmes Community based Research and Action Partnerships for Systemic Change Digital platforms for Changemaking networks About Us Our Story Our People Legal & Compliances Publications Community Solutions & Case Studies Health & Livelihoods Policies & Programmes Training, Networks & WQCs Water Quality Monitoring Water-Safe Fundamentals Media Publications Films Gallery Connect Together, मिलकर મળીને একেলগে মিলি ಜೊತೆಯಲ್ಲಿ একসাথে let''s save lives through simple ideas. Who We Are INREM Foundation works at the intersection of climate, water, and public health to build water-safe communities across India. We bring together people, science, and systems to ensure that every household has access to safe water and a healthier future. Our vision is to enable a network of one million Water Quality Champions by 2030. These are ASHA and Anganwadi frontline workers, students, teachers and community leaders who take ownership of water safety in their villages. Equipped with the right tools, local and accessible data and knowledge, innovative solutions, and expert mentoring, they identify and address water quality challenges in their communities. We believe', 'Central India', null, null, null, 'India', 'hello@inremfoundation.org', '17781807832', 'https://inremfoundation.org', '{"youtube": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=6eAYA04jVmk", "facebook": "https://www.facebook.com/inremfoundation", "twitter": "https://twitter.com/inremwater", "linkedin": "https://www.linkedin.com/company/inrem-foundation"}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Water', 'Health', 'Rural Development', 'Central India', 'Grassroot/Implementation CSOs', 'CRA Partner Map workbook', 'Water quality', 'Rural WASH', 'West India']::text[], ARRAY['Water', 'Health', 'Rural Development', 'Central India', '