Reviewed pages: https://fieldsofview.in; https://fieldsofview.in/about', 'approved', now(), 'admin', false, 'Fields of View Fields of View aims to undertake research at the intersection of technology, social sciences, and art to design these tools for policymakers and people. About - Fields of View Skip to main content about partners team board alumni tools E-QLT Jee-van Weather Wane Scheme! Reimagining Resilience resources publications newsletters financials archive publications newsletters financials archive get involved About Partners Team Board Alumni We are an inter-disciplinary team developing games, simulations, and workshops to engage with wicked problems. For the last 12 years, we have been making tools to help individuals, organisations, and policymakers understand the messiness and complexity of their landscapes. We focus on addressing vulnerability through data-informed and participatory policy-making. learn more about our tools Meet our partners Meet our team Anirudh G Communications Email LinkedIn Anirudh is a Bangalore-based social worker interested in the use of language and dialogue for collective action. They have been a part of grassroots movements since 2018, focusing on systemic change for the advancement of minority rights. They aim to leverage their understanding of the social sector to help FoV expand its reach and amplify its impact. Anirudh enjoys cooking, solving puzzles, and deep dives into mundane topics. anirudh@fieldsofvie South India India 1. Citizen engagement representation in climate governance 2. Making climate conversations accessible to all (de-jargonize climate to scale awareness) 3. Strengthening government capacity understanding on climate 4. Integration of technology in climate governance South India Think Tanks CRA Partner Map workbook 1. Citizen engagement representation in climate governance 2. Making climate conversations accessible to all (de-jargonize climate to scale awareness) 3. Strengthening government capacity und