Reviewed pages: https://socratus.org; https://socratus.org/contact; https://socratus.org/contact-us; https://socratus.org/about; https://socratus.org/about-us', 'approved', now(), 'admin', false, 'Socratus Socratus Foundation is a think-tank dedicated towards harnessing collective wisdom to tackle wicked problems seen in today''s society. SOCRATUS SOCRATUS News Products Partners About Midwifing Collective Wisdom A studio for thinking through and solving wicked problems The world has many ''wicked'' problems that defy easy solutions. These problems are systemic, interrelated and intractable. We need collective wisdom to engage with the wickedness. This wisdom exists amongst us. However, it needs to be surfaced. We bring together the ''right'' people to carefully designed spaces. Over time we prototype some ideas emerging from these spaces. We also produce and distribute tools to imagine, think and solve. Socratus seeks to midwife the collective wisdom that is needed. Socratus strives for a flourishing society on a thriving planet. We think through products and spaces. We create process and tools as our products for planetary commons. Menu Wystem EPI (Ecosystem Programming Interface) We are attempting to build an EPI (ecosystem programming interface) with our wisdom system, or Wystem as we call it, that uses computational concepts to help us build more robust ecosystems: recipes, exchanges and interfaces. Citizen Juries It is a space in which a jury comprised of regular people sit in judgement of policies made for them. E Pan-India, India India 1. Narrative Building 2. Convenings around livelihood food and climate change. Pan-India India Think Tanks CRA Partner Map workbook 1. Narrative Building 2. Convenings around livelihood food and climate change. Pan-India India Think Tanks Socratus 1. Narrative Building 2. Convenings around livelihood food and climate change. Farmers Communities Pan-India India Society SOCRATUS SOCRATUS News Products Partners About Midwifing Collective Wisdom A studio for thinking through and solving wicked problems The world has many ''wicked'' problems that defy easy solutions.', now()),
('cso-centre-for-study-of-science-technology-and-policy-cstep-8571417d', 'Centre for study of Science, Technology and Policy (CSTEP)', 'CSTEP is one of India''s leading think tanks, with a mission to enrich policymaking with innovative approaches using science and technology.', 'Home Page - CSTEP Home Page Home Who We Are About Us Our Team Mission & Vision Our Work Clean Air For All India''s Green Energy Transition Sustainable and Secure Future Digital Transformation Projects Resources Publications News Blogs Tools Multimedia Events Careers Essence We work with governments and institutions to develop solutions using science and technology. About us Laid Waste Legacy dumpsites are posing a grave environmental, health, and urban challenge for most Indian cities. Read Our Issue Brief Checks and Balances Low-cost sensors need to undergo regular checks to factor in meteorological conditions and pollutant compositions. Read our report The Carbon Saga Our study explores how carbon capture, utilisation, and storage can help decarbonise industries in India. Read more Future Gazing Our blog series, Thinking in Models, unpacks NITI Aayog''s multisectoral modelling reports that explore the scenarios shaping India''s pathways to Viksit Bharat and net zero. Read the first blog Gritty at 20 Our Annual Report 2024-25 traces the evolution of bold ideas into practical solutions at scale. Read More About CSTEP The Center for Study of Science, Technology and Policy (CSTEP) is a', 'Nagashettyhalli (RMV II Stage), Karnataka', 'No. 18, 10th Cross, Mayura Street, Papanna Layout, Nagashettyhalli (RMV II Stage), Bengaluru 560094 Karnataka, India', 'Nagashettyhalli (RMV II Stage)', 'Karnataka', 'India', 'cpe@cstep.in', '18.8201 18.3685', 'https://cstep.in/', '{"twitter": "https://twitter.com/CSTEP_India", "youtube": "https://www.youtube.com/channel/UCROj7dD9PqkZj4My5En829A", "instagram": "https://www.instagram.com/cstep_ind", "linkedin": "http://www.linkedin.com/company/cstep"}'::jsonb, '["1st Floor, Tower-A, Smartworks Corporate Park, Sector-125, Noida 201303 Uttar Pradesh, India", "Bengaluru, founded in", "It conducted SAFARI (Sustainable Alternative Futures for India) modelling studies to explore sustainable development pathways aligned with the UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs).", "CSTEP won the India Smart Grid Forum Innovation Award 2020 for implementing a smart microgrid project in Kudagaon, Odisha.", "CSTEP established a new regional office in Noida, expanding its footprint in Northern India and enabling greater engagement with national policy institutions."]'::jsonb, ARRAY['1.Air pollution 2. Heat Stress 3.Energy Transition 4.Risk and vulnerability assessment (at decentralized levels)', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Think Tanks', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['1.Air pollution 2. Heat Stress 3.Energy Transition 4.Risk and vulnerability assessment (at decentralized levels)', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Think Tanks', 'Centre for study of Science, Technology and Policy (CSTEP)']::text[], 12.9617437, 77.7168019, 'CRA Partner Map workbook', 'https://cstep.in/', '{"areas_of_work": ["1.Air pollution 2. Heat Stress 3.Energy Transition 4.Risk and vulnerability assessment (at decentralized levels)"], "beneficiary_groups": ["Women", "Children"], "geography_served": ["Pan-India", "India"], "registration_status": "Section 8", "registration_number": null, "programs": "Home Page - CSTEP Home Page Home Who We Are About Us Our Team Mission & Vision Our Work Clean Air For All India''s Green Energy Transition Sustainable and Secure Future Digital Transformation Projects Resources Publications News Blogs Tools Multimedia Events Careers Essence We work with governments and institutions to develop solutions using science and technology.", "volunteer_or_partner_needs": null}'::jsonb, 'CRA partner import', 'tanmay@greenruraleconomy.in', 'Source workbook category: Think Tanks
