Reviewed pages: https://www.youcan.in/; https://www.youcan.in/the-initiative; https://www.youcan.in/programmes; https://www.youcan.in/people', 'approved', now(), 'admin', false, 'YouCan YouCan Foundation empowers young people to drive social change through leadership, volunteering, and advocacy, including environmental initiatives. Home | YouCAN Website top of page Home About Us People Programs Fellowship Report Cohort 4 Fellows Testimonials Resources Blog Connect Alumni More Use tab to navigate through the menu items. EEF 4.0 Snapshot out now! Click to read Invest in Educators for a prosperous India Here''s How Inspire. Empower. Nurture. Environmental apathy is the root cause of the climate crisis. Still, most of India''s largest demographic - the 260 million K-12 students complete school without connecting with nature and knowing the intricacies of climate change. That''s why YouCAN functions as a mission-driven non-profit organisation founded with the vision of an Earth Educator in every school and learning space in India. We improve opportunities for K-12 students to connect with nature locally and practice climate action during their formative years. YouCAN is an initiative of the Trust for Environmental Education. Read Founders'' Note Our Program Earth Educators Fellowship Enquire with us The Earth Educators Fellowship brings together 20 young environmentalists, emerging grassroots conservationists, school teachers, and informal educators who have an enterprising spirit to challenge the status quo of nature Pan-India, India India Youth Leadership Environment Civic Action Pan-India India Media/Citizen Engagement CRA Partner Map workbook Youth Leadership Environment Civic Action Pan-India India Media/Citizen Engagement YouCan Social Media Written https://www.instagram.com/youcanedu https://www.facebook.com/youcanedu https://www.youcan.in/ Twitter | https://twitter.com/youcanedu Pan-India India Women Youth Children Communities Rural communities https://www.youcan.in/blog', now()),
('story_teller-peoples-archive-of-rural-india-pari-4d58f952', 'People''s Archive of Rural India (PARI)', 'PARI is a living journal and archive documenting the diverse lives of everyday India through stories, photographs, and videos. Exploring issues of rural India - agriculture, labor, climate change, and the lives of marginalized communities.', 'PARI - People''s Archive of Rural India Loading header... EN | English 6 languages SUNDAY, MAY 10, 2026 Toggle menu Explore Donate Toggle theme Dismiss Welcome to PARI! Let''s get you acquainted Welcome to PARI! Let''s get you acquainted The People''s Archive of Rural India PARI is about the everyday lives of everyday people. Rural India is the most diverse part of the planet. Its 833 million humans speak close to 800 languages and share millions of livelihoods, arts, cultures, literature and legends... Read more Many worlds, myriad tongues PARI publishes in 15 languages spoken by 1.2 billion Indians and identified by them as their mother tongue. This is the largest multilingual journalistic endeavour in the world - treating all languages on the site as equal... Read more PARI Library PARI doesn''t just lend you reports, documents and books - it gives them away to you to download free of charge. The PARI Library has reports, important gazettes, out-of-print books, rare documents and lots more… Go to the library Donate! Support rural journalism PARI needs your help to pull off this most ambitious of Indian journalistic endeavours. We need you to fund us to cover your country. Contribute', 'Mumbai, Maharashtra', 'Bandra West, Mumbai, Maharashtra- 400050', 'Mumbai', 'Maharashtra', 'India', 'psainath@ruralindiaonline.org', '4.93 4.93 1.41 1.41', 'https://ruralindiaonline.org/', '{}'::jsonb, '[]'::jsonb, ARRAY['Rural Journalism', 'Culture', 'Livelihoods', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Media/Citizen Engagement', 'CRA Partner Map workbook']::text[], ARRAY['Rural Journalism', 'Culture', 'Livelihoods', 'Pan-India', 'India', 'Media/Citizen 